# MCP Accessibility Testing - Cursor Integration

This MCP server provides 64 comprehensive accessibility testing tools for WCAG 2.1 compliance testing.

## 🔨 Available Tool Categories

### Browser Control (8 tools)
- `open_browser` - Launch browser
- `navigate` - Navigate to URL
- `click` - Click elements
- `fill` - Fill form inputs
- `login` - Automated login
- `screenshot` - Capture screenshots
- `close_browser` - Close browser
- `wait` - Wait for conditions

### Core Accessibility Testing (23 tools)
- `analyze_accessibility` - Full WCAG audit with axe-core
- `get_accessibility_tree` - Inspect accessibility tree
- `simulate_screen_reader` - Simulate NVDA/JAWS/VoiceOver
- `test_keyboard_navigation` - Test keyboard accessibility
- `validate_aria_attributes` - Check ARIA usage
- `get_landmarks` - Find ARIA landmarks
- `test_form_labels` - Validate form accessibility
- `test_heading_structure` - Check heading hierarchy
- `test_skip_links` - Validate skip navigation
- `test_live_regions` - Test dynamic content
- `get_focus_order` - Map tab order
- `test_focus_trap` - Detect focus traps
- `test_tab_order` - Verify tab sequence
- `get_announcements` - Capture screen reader announcements
- `get_semantic_structure` - Analyze semantic HTML
- `get_accessible_name` - Get accessible names
- Plus element discovery and inspection tools

### Platform-Specific Testing (10 tools)
Test cross-platform screen reader compatibility:
- `test_screen_reader_modes` - Browse/Forms/Application modes
- `test_platform_aria_support` - Compare ARIA across platforms
- `test_high_contrast` - Windows/Mac contrast modes
- `test_table_navigation` - Platform table patterns
- `test_verbosity_levels` - Screen reader verbosity
- `test_quick_navigation` - Single-letter navigation (H, B, F, T)
- `test_virtual_buffer` - Windows virtual cursor
- `test_rotor_navigation` - VoiceOver rotor (VO+U)
- `get_platform_announcements` - Platform-specific announcements
- `test_math_content` - Mathematical content (MathML/LaTeX)

### Widget Keyboard Testing (13 tools)
Test ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG) patterns:
- `test_tabs_widget` - Tabs pattern (arrow keys, auto-activation)
- `test_accordion_widget` - Accordion (Enter/Space, arrows)
- `test_combobox_widget` - Combobox (Alt+Down, Escape)
- `test_slider_widget` - Slider (arrows, Home/End, Page Up/Down)
- `test_menu_widget` - Menu/menubar (arrows, Enter, Escape)
- `test_listbox_widget` - Listbox (arrows, multi-select)
- `test_radio_group_widget` - Radio group (arrows with auto-check)
- `test_tree_widget` - Tree (arrows, Enter, *, expand/collapse)
- `test_modal_dialog_widget` - Modal (focus trap, Escape, initial focus)
- `test_date_picker_widget` - Date picker (calendar navigation)
- `test_data_table_widget` - Data table/grid (sorting, filtering)
- `test_carousel_widget` - Carousel (arrows, pause, auto-rotate)
- `test_toolbar_widget` - Toolbar (arrows, Home/End, Tab)

### Visual & Responsive Testing (10 tools)
Test WCAG 2.1 visual criteria:
- `test_focus_visibility` - Focus indicators (3:1 contrast, 2px size) - WCAG 2.4.7, 2.4.13
- `test_hover_focus_dismissal` - Hover content (hoverable, dismissible) - WCAG 1.4.13
- `test_reflow` - Content reflow (320px, no horizontal scroll) - WCAG 1.4.10
- `test_text_resize` - Text at 200% zoom (no content loss) - WCAG 1.4.4
- `test_text_spacing` - Text spacing (line-height, letter/word spacing) - WCAG 1.4.12
- `test_auto_refresh` - Auto-refresh/redirects - WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.2.1 (Timing Adjustable) - Level A
- `test_animation_control` - Animation controls (pause, stop, hide) - WCAG 2.1 Success Criteria 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide) - Level A, and 2.3.3 (Animation from Interactions) - Level AAA
- `test_error_messages` - Error accessibility (visible, announced) - WCAG 3.3.1, 4.1.3
- `test_required_fields` - Required indicators (aria-required) - WCAG 3.3.2
- `test_orientation_lock` - Orientation support (portrait/landscape) - WCAG 1.3.4

## 🚀 Recommended Testing Workflow

### Quick WCAG Scan
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. analyze_accessibility - Get full WCAG 2.1 AA report
4. screenshot - Capture evidence
5. close_browser
```

### Comprehensive Testing
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. analyze_accessibility - Axe-core scan
4. test_keyboard_navigation - Tab through page
5. get_focus_order - Verify focus sequence
6. test_heading_structure - Check heading hierarchy
7. validate_aria_attributes - Verify ARIA usage
8. test_form_labels - Check form accessibility
9. get_landmarks - Find page regions
10. screenshot
11. close_browser
```

### Platform-Specific Testing (Mac VoiceOver)
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. test_screen_reader_modes - Test Browse/Forms/Application modes
4. test_rotor_navigation - Test VoiceOver rotor
5. test_high_contrast - Test Mac Increase Contrast
6. get_platform_announcements - Get VoiceOver announcements
7. test_math_content - Test math content (if applicable)
8. close_browser
```

### Platform-Specific Testing (Windows JAWS/NVDA)
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. test_screen_reader_modes - Test Browse/Forms modes
4. test_virtual_buffer - Test virtual cursor
5. test_quick_navigation - Test single-letter nav (H, B, F, T)
6. test_high_contrast - Test Windows High Contrast
7. test_verbosity_levels - Test verbosity settings
8. close_browser
```

### Widget Testing
For pages with ARIA widgets (tabs, accordions, menus, etc.):
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. test_tabs_widget - If page has tabs
4. test_accordion_widget - If page has accordions
5. test_combobox_widget - If page has comboboxes/dropdowns
6. test_menu_widget - If page has menus
7. test_modal_dialog_widget - If page has modals
8. test_date_picker_widget - If page has date pickers
9. close_browser
```

### Visual/Responsive Testing
For WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance:
```
1. open_browser
2. navigate to [URL]
3. test_focus_visibility - Check focus indicators
4. test_reflow - Test at 320px width
5. test_text_resize - Test at 200% zoom
6. test_text_spacing - Test increased spacing
7. test_orientation_lock - Test portrait/landscape
8. test_animation_control - Check animation controls
9. test_error_messages - Verify error accessibility
10. test_required_fields - Check required field indicators
11. close_browser
```

## 📝 Best Practices

### Always Test in Sequence
1. **Start with automated scan**: `analyze_accessibility` gives comprehensive WCAG report
2. **Test keyboard navigation**: Verify keyboard-only users can access everything
3. **Test screen reader compatibility**: Use platform-specific tools
4. **Test visual criteria**: Focus visibility, reflow, text resize
5. **Test widgets**: Use specific widget tests for ARIA components

### When to Use Which Tools

**Use `analyze_accessibility` when:**
- You need a comprehensive WCAG 2.1 AA audit
- Starting a new accessibility review
- Need detailed violation reports with WCAG references

**Use `simulate_screen_reader` when:**
- You want to see what screen reader users hear
- Testing specific element announcements
- Verifying ARIA labels and descriptions

**Use widget-specific tools when:**
- Page has ARIA widgets (tabs, accordions, menus, etc.)
- Need to verify keyboard patterns match APG
- Testing complex interactive components

**Use platform-specific tools when:**
- Testing cross-platform compatibility
- Need to verify behavior on specific screen readers (JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver)
- Testing platform-specific features (virtual buffer, rotor)

**Use visual/responsive tools when:**
- Testing WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance
- Verifying focus indicators, reflow, text spacing
- Testing responsive design accessibility

### Persistent Browser Sessions

If you need to test authenticated pages, use persistent Chrome profiles:

1. Set environment variable before starting:
   ```bash
   export CHROME_USER_DATA_DIR="$HOME/.chrome-profiles/mcp-accessibility"
   ```

2. Or configure in Claude Desktop/Cursor MCP settings:
   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "mcp-accessibility": {
         "command": "node",
         "args": ["./mcp/dist/index.js"],
         "env": {
           "CHROME_USER_DATA_DIR": "/Users/yourname/.chrome-profiles/mcp-accessibility"
         }
       }
     }
   }
   ```

3. Log in once manually, session persists across tests

## 🎯 Common Testing Scenarios

### Scenario 1: New Feature Accessibility Review
Run comprehensive test suite:
- Automated WCAG scan
- Keyboard navigation
- Screen reader simulation
- Widget testing (if applicable)
- Visual/responsive testing
- Take screenshots for documentation

### Scenario 2: Bug Fix Verification
Focus on specific area:
- Test the specific component/page
- Run relevant widget tests
- Verify ARIA attributes
- Test keyboard navigation for that component
- Screenshot before/after

### Scenario 3: Cross-Platform Compatibility
Test on multiple platforms:
- Mac VoiceOver specific tests
- Windows JAWS/NVDA specific tests
- Compare platform announcements
- Test high contrast on both platforms

### Scenario 4: WCAG 2.1 Compliance Audit
Run full visual/responsive suite:
- Focus visibility
- Reflow at 320px
- Text resize at 200%
- Text spacing customization
- Orientation support
- Animation controls
- Error message accessibility

## 🔍 Understanding Tool Output

All tools return structured results with:
- **Summary**: High-level overview of findings
- **Issues**: Detailed list of accessibility problems
- **WCAG References**: Which success criteria are affected
- **Recommendations**: How to fix the issues
- **Code Examples**: Where available

## ⚠️ Important Notes

- Always `open_browser` before testing
- Always `close_browser` when done to free resources
- Use `screenshot` to capture evidence
- Test one page thoroughly rather than many pages superficially
- Focus on high-severity issues first (Critical, Serious)
- Verify fixes don't introduce new accessibility issues

## 🆘 Troubleshooting

**Browser won't start:**
- Check if Playwright is installed: `npx playwright install chromium`
- Verify MCP server is running

**Tools timing out:**
- Complex pages may take longer to analyze
- Wait for page to fully load before testing
- Use `wait` tool if needed

**Persistent session not working:**
- Verify CHROME_USER_DATA_DIR path is correct
- Ensure directory has write permissions
- Log in again manually if session expired

